            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex pattern to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nThe pattern works as follows:\n\n- **`^(?=...IPv4...)`** - Lookahead ensures the line contains an IPv4 address with proper word boundaries\n- **`.*`** - Greedy match to position just before the last date (due to backtracking)\n- **`(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01]))(?![A-Za-z0-9])`** - Captures the date with word boundaries:\n  - Month: `0[1-9]|1[0-2]` → 01-12\n  - Day: `0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01]` → 01-31 (includes Feb 29)\n- **`.*$`** - Matches remaining characters to end of line\n\nThe IPv4 octet pattern `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d{2}|[1-9]?\\d)` correctly matches 0-255 without leading zeros. The negative lookbehind/lookahead assertions prevent false matches like \"user 1234-12-1234\"."
